    <div class="intro-box">
      <h3>💡 What is this module?</h3>
      <p>The <strong>graph</strong> module defines <code>AgentState</code> — the single shared data structure that every agent in the LangGraph workflow reads from and writes to. It also provides utility functions for debug output.</p>
      <p class="analogy">"Think of it as a <strong>shared whiteboard in a conference room</strong> — each analyst walks up, reads what others have written, adds their own notes, and the whiteboard keeps everything organized. The <code>Annotated</code> reducers ensure that notes are <em>accumulated</em> (messages) or <em>merged</em> (data/metadata) rather than overwritten."</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="toc" id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2></nav>

    <h2 id="architecture">Architecture Overview</h2>
    <p>At the centre of LangGraph's execution model is a state object passed between nodes. <code>AgentState</code> is that object for the AI Hedge Fund — a TypedDict with three annotated fields whose reducers control how concurrent writes are reconciled.</p>
    <div class="mermaid-wrapper" onclick="openOverlay(this)">
      <pre class="mermaid" data-source="graph TD
    A[LangGraph Runtime] -->|passes state| B[AgentState TypedDict]
    B --> C[messages: list — operator.add reducer]
    B --> D[data: dict — merge_dicts reducer]
    B --> E[metadata: dict — merge_dicts reducer]
    C --> F[Analyst Agent 1]
    C --> G[Analyst Agent 2]
    C --> H[Portfolio Manager]
    D --> F
    D --> G
    D --> H
    F -->|returns partial state| A
    G -->|returns partial state| A
    H -->|returns partial state| A
    style B fill:#58a6ff,stroke:#333,color:#000
    style A fill:#3fb950,stroke:#333,color:#000">graph TD
    A[LangGraph Runtime] -->|passes state| B[AgentState TypedDict]
    B --> C[messages: list — operator.add reducer]
    B --> D[data: dict — merge_dicts reducer]
    B --> E[metadata: dict — merge_dicts reducer]
    C --> F[Analyst Agent 1]
