    <h2 id="data-flow">State Data Flow</h2>
    <p>Each agent node receives the full <code>AgentState</code>, reads what it needs, and returns a partial state dict. LangGraph uses the annotated reducers to merge the partial return into the accumulated state before passing it to the next node.</p>
    <div class="mermaid-wrapper" onclick="openOverlay(this)">
      <pre class="mermaid" data-source="sequenceDiagram
    participant LG as LangGraph Runtime
    participant A1 as Analyst Agent
    participant A2 as Risk Manager
    participant PM as Portfolio Manager
    LG->>A1: AgentState {messages:[], data:{tickers}, metadata:{}}
    A1->>A1: Analyze tickers, produce signals
    A1-->>LG: {messages:[HumanMessage], data:{analyst_signals: {...}}}
    Note over LG: operator.add merges messages, merge_dicts merges data
    LG->>A2: AgentState {messages:[...], data:{tickers, analyst_signals}}
    A2-->>LG: {messages:[...], data:{risk_assessment: {...}}}
    LG->>PM: AgentState with all accumulated data
    PM-->>LG: {messages:[...], data:{portfolio_decision: {...}}}">sequenceDiagram
    participant LG as LangGraph Runtime
    participant A1 as Analyst Agent
    participant A2 as Risk Manager
    participant PM as Portfolio Manager
    LG->>A1: AgentState {messages:[], data:{tickers}, metadata:{}}
    A1->>A1: Analyze tickers, produce signals
    A1-->>LG: {messages:[HumanMessage], data:{analyst_signals: {...}}}
    Note over LG: operator.add merges messages, merge_dicts merges data
    LG->>A2: AgentState {messages:[...], data:{tickers, analyst_signals}}
    A2-->>LG: {messages:[...], data:{risk_assessment: {...}}}
    LG->>PM: AgentState with all accumulated data
    PM-->>LG: {messages:[...], data:{portfolio_decision: {...}}}</pre>
    </div>

