    <h2 id="deep-dive">Deep Dive</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>📝 AgentState TypedDict</h4>
        <p>Only 3 fields, but they carry the entire workflow's state. The <code>messages</code> list grows with each agent's output; <code>data</code> accumulates tickers, signals, and portfolio decisions; <code>metadata</code> holds config.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🔀 Reducer Pattern</h4>
        <p>LangGraph's <code>Annotated</code> trick: by attaching <code>operator.add</code> to messages, each agent's returned messages are <em>appended</em> rather than overwriting. Similarly, <code>merge_dicts</code> shallow-merges data dicts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🐛 Debug Utilities</h4>
        <p><code>show_agent_reasoning()</code> prints formatted JSON when <code>metadata.show_reasoning</code> is True. Uses <code>convert_to_serializable()</code> to handle Pydantic models and datetime objects.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>⚡ Minimal Footprint</h4>
        <p>At just 51 lines, this is the smallest module — yet it's the most critical. Every other module depends on this state contract to communicate through the workflow.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

